Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] misc: fastrpc: forward-port DSP signal (dspsignal) support to 7.2.9

Forward-port of the unmerged 2024 series patch
"[PATCH v1 14/16] misc: fastrpc: Add DSP signal support"
(Ekansh Gupta, Anandu Krishnan E; Qualcomm), patchwork id 13542157,
Message-ID <20240202064039.15505-15-quic_ekangupt@quicinc.com>.

Differences from the 2024 patch (mainline has no multimode-invoke ioctl,
so this cannot be a straight cherry-pick):
 - exposed through a dedicated ioctl FASTRPC_IOCTL_DSPSIGNAL
   _IOWR('R', 0x40, struct fastrpc_ioctl_dspsignal) - a PRIVATE number,
   not upstream ABI; needs the matching libcdsprpc patch in
   patches/fastrpc-userspace/
 - req 0 (QUERY) lets userspace probe for support
 - DSP <-> CPU signal message uses fl->client_id (what mainline sends to
   the DSP as the process id) instead of tgid
 - 8-byte signal messages are handled before the "len < sizeof(rsp)"
   check in the rpmsg callback (mainline would otherwise drop them)
 - receiver looks the user up under cctx->lock and does not dereference
   a missing user (the 2024 code did when no user matched)
 - wait timeout compares the microsecond value, not jiffies, against
   the "no timeout" sentinel
 - signal groups are freed in fastrpc_user_free()

Applies on top of 0001 (PD-exit v2). Build-tested on 7.2.9 (arm64).
NOT yet boot-tested at the time of publishing.
Note: qualcomm/fastrpc#377 reports that a dspsignal backport alone did
not cure the hang on X2 Elite (glymur); X1E results are pending.
